========================================================================
E3 BORROWER ARCHETYPE (KMeans + production lookup)
========================================================================
Training data: External_Cibil_Dataset.csv (51336, 63)
Features used: NETMONTHLYINCOME, AGE, Time_With_Curr_Empr, EDUCATION
Dropped: GENDER, MARITALSTATUS, Credit_Score, Approved_Flag, all 50+ other columns
GENDER distribution in kept rows: {'M': 45245, 'F': 6091}
MARITALSTATUS: {'Married': 37752, 'Single': 13584}
EDUCATION: {'GRADUATE': 16673, '12TH': 14467, 'SSC': 9276, 'UNDER GRADUATE': 5492, 'OTHERS': 2917, 'POST-GRADUATE': 2242, 'PROFESSIONAL': 269}

Training script: scripts/train_borrower_archetype.py
  - n_clusters=4, random_state=42
  - Cluster labeling by centroid ranking: highest education='Educated Professionals', highest tenure='Highly Tenured Veterans', lowest age of remaining='Young Starters'
  - Education Ordinal Map: 8 categories from OTHERS to PROFESSIONAL
  - Save to: data/processed/borrower_archetype_definitions.json

Rows after dropna + map: 51336
Cluster sizes: [19963 20292 11080     1]
Inertia: 110690
Silhouette: 0.283
Calinski-Harabasz: 14632

Centroids (unscaled):
   NETMONTHLYINCOME        AGE  Time_With_Curr_Empr  EDUCATION
0      2.649950e+04  29.913374            81.110711   3.906064
1      2.282158e+04  31.488874            87.573247   1.420289
2      3.264534e+04  44.824547           206.231774   2.469586
3      2.500000e+06  25.000000            35.000000   4.000000

Assigned labels (per training script):
  Cluster 3 → 'Educated Professionals': n=1, GENDER M%=100.0, mean age=25.0
  Cluster 2 → 'Highly Tenured Veterans': n=11080, GENDER M%=87.9, mean age=44.8
  Cluster 0 → 'Young Starters': n=19963, GENDER M%=89.3, mean age=29.9
  Cluster 1 → 'Mid-Career Established': n=20292, GENDER M%=87.1, mean age=31.5

PRODUCTION PATH: livelihood_mapper.py is a STRING LOOKUP, not the KMeans.
Cluster labels are NOT used in production. The 4 labels in borrower_archetype_definitions.json are display-only fallbacks.
Person A engine loads neither kmeans_model.pkl nor definitions.json.
Person B engine does not call get_borrower_archetype at all (only E6 livelihood_mapper).

========================================================================
E5 READINESS
========================================================================
No ML model in models/readiness/ (empty). Pure rule-based scoring.
models/readiness contents: ['.gitkeep']
Implementation: backend/app/engines/readiness/readiness_engine.py — explicit weighted scoring, no model artifacts.
Floor breach override at financial_health_score < 0.5 hard-codes band='Not Ready' regardless of other components.

Training data: data/processed/readiness_data.csv (40,000 rows, Person B schema)
Columns: ['city', 'age', 'sex', 'social_class', 'primary_business', 'secondary_business', 'annual_income', 'monthly_expenses', 'old_dependents', 'young_dependents', 'home_ownership', 'type_of_house', 'occupants_count', 'house_area', 'sanitary_availability', 'water_availability', 'loan_purpose', 'loan_tenure', 'loan_installments', 'loan_amount']
Shape: (40000, 20)

No target column. Rules are hand-coded in readiness_engine.py.
Calibration: cannot calibrate (no ground truth to calibrate against).
Synthetic labels: not applicable (no model).
Fairness: social_class and sex are in the data but NOT used by the engine.
Bands: Ready / Moderately Ready / Needs Improvement / Not Ready (hard thresholds 75/50/25).

========================================================================
E6 LIVELIHOOD
========================================================================
data/processed/livelihood_data.csv: 100+ one-hot macro columns, 1 row = 1 applicant
Shape: (40000, 20)
Columns: ['city', 'age', 'sex', 'social_class', 'primary_business', 'secondary_business', 'annual_income', 'monthly_expenses', 'old_dependents', 'young_dependents', 'home_ownership', 'type_of_house', 'occupants_count', 'house_area', 'sanitary_availability', 'water_availability', 'loan_purpose', 'loan_tenure', 'loan_installments', 'loan_amount']

Implementation: backend/app/engines/livelihood/livelihood_mapper.py
Method: pure dictionary lookup on 'primary_business' string. No model.
6 archetypes: General Micro-Enterprise, Trade & Retail, Services, Agri-Allied, Manufacturing, Transport & Logistics
Cluster 0 (General Micro-Enterprise) is the catch-all default when no key matches.
Signature: only accepts a string, explicitly not the applicant dict. See mapper.py:75-77.

